Reason: every enemy calls instance_activate_region each step, and each call reads the box of every inactive instance:
in the water room ~8.5 calls a frame over ~285 inactive solids, 0.7 ms of a 8.4 ms step (Dolphin, emulated time).
Nearly all are memo hits (patch 0045), but GCC kept Collision_computeBBox out of line with the miss path's state
spilled to the stack, ~150 instructions per hit. The hit test is now its own always-inline function, used directly by
instance_activate_region and instance_deactivate_region; a miss falls back to Collision_computeBBox, which runs the
same test and stores the box as before. The comparisons and the stored values are unchanged.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

